' --- Diagrama: mapa de autenticação e tokens ---
@startuml
title Mapa de autenticação — tokens e credenciais
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor "Analista" as U

package "Cliente" #E8F5E9 {
  [Frontend React\nVITE_API_TOKEN] as FE
  [WPF Desktop] as WPF
}

package "API host" #E3F2FD {
  [Backend FastAPI\nRATANALYZER_API_TOKEN] as API
  [upload_security.py] as UP
}

package "Sandbox" #FFE0B2 {
  [vm-agent\nVM_AGENT_TOKEN] as AGENT
  [Scripts Hyper-V\nPROJETOVM_Guest*] as PS
}

database "secrets/\nbackend.env" as SEC

U --> FE
U --> WPF

' *Token API partilhado entre clientes e backend*
FE --> API : X-API-Token
WPF --> API : X-API-Token
WPF --> PS : credenciais guest
API --> UP : validar uploads
API --> AGENT : X-Agent-Token\n(driver hyperv)

' *Fonte única de segredos em secrets/backend.env*
SEC ..> API : RATANALYZER_API_TOKEN
SEC ..> FE : build-time token
SEC ..> AGENT : VM_AGENT_TOKEN
SEC ..> PS : PROJETOVM_GuestPassword

note right of API
  **Fail-closed** em produção:
  RATANALYZER_ENV=production
  exige token válido
end note

note bottom of AGENT
  Comparação em tempo constante
  (TokenComparer.cs)
end note

note bottom of PS
  PowerShell Direct —
  sem token HTTP;
  password obrigatória
  (exceto flag dev)
end note

' *Driver stub não executa amostras nem requer auth*
rectangle "Driver stub" as STUB #F5F5F5
API ..> STUB : sem auth\n(não executa amostras)

@enduml
